'''Maiwala''' is an [[Oceanic language]] of [[Milne Bay Province]], [[Papua New Guinea]].

The Maiwala language has 13 consonants: b, d, {{IPA|ɡ}}, {{IPA link|ɣ}} {{angle bracket|gh}}, h, k, {{IPA link|ɺ}} {{angle bracket|l}}, m, n, p, s, t, v; two semi-vowels: w, {{IPA link|j}} {{angle bracket|y}}; and five vowels: {{IPA link|a}}, {{IPA link|ɛ}} {{angle bracket|e}}, {{IPA link|ɪ}} {{angle bracket|i}}, {{IPA link|ɔ}} {{angle bracket|o}}, {{IPA link|ʊ}} {{angle bracket|u}}.<ref>Nagai 2003:126</ref>

